.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH rpmcrab 1  "rpmcrab 0.1.0" 
.SH NAME
rpmcrab \- Check for common problems in rpm packages
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrpmcrab\fR [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] [\fB\-c\fR|\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-e\fR|\fB\-\-explain\fR] [\fB\-r\fR|\fB\-\-rpmlintrc\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-p\fR|\fB\-\-print\-config\fR] [\fB\-i\fR|\fB\-\-installed\fR] [\fB\-t\fR|\fB\-\-time\-report\fR] [\fB\-j\fR|\fB\-\-jobs\fR] [\fB\-\-ignore\-unused\-rpmlintrc\fR] [\fB\-\-checks\fR] [\fB\-s\fR|\fB\-\-strict\fR] [\fB\-\-errors\-only\fR] [\fB\-P\fR|\fB\-\-permissive\fR] [\fB\-m\fR|\fB\-\-mini\-mode\fR] [\fB\-\-format\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fIrpmfile\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Check for common problems in rpm packages
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version and exit
.TP
\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-config\fR \fI<path>\fR
Config file or directory of `*.toml` (repeatable)
.TP
\fB\-e\fR, \fB\-\-explain\fR \fI<id>...\fR
Print the description for a message id and exit
.TP
\fB\-r\fR, \fB\-\-rpmlintrc\fR \fI<path>\fR
A rpmlintrc file (repeatable)
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Inline explanations (and re\-raise internal errors)
.TP
\fB\-p\fR, \fB\-\-print\-config\fR
Dump the merged configuration as TOML and exit
.TP
\fB\-i\fR, \fB\-\-installed\fR \fI<name>...\fR
Check installed RPM DB packages
.TP
\fB\-t\fR, \fB\-\-time\-report\fR
Per\-check timing report
.TP
\fB\-j\fR, \fB\-\-jobs\fR \fI<n>\fR
Number of parallel worker threads for checking packages; 1 is sequential. Defaults to the machine\*(Aqs parallelism
.TP
\fB\-\-ignore\-unused\-rpmlintrc\fR
Suppress the `unused\-rpmlintrc\-filter` audit
.TP
\fB\-\-checks\fR \fI<a,b,c>\fR
Run only these checks (debug)
.TP
\fB\-s\fR, \fB\-\-strict\fR
Treat all messages as errors
.TP
\fB\-\-errors\-only\fR
Skip warning\-only checks entirely (upstream rpmlint#134). A static pre\-scoring bound on each check\*(Aqs declared max severity; disabled under \-\-strict
.TP
\fB\-P\fR, \fB\-\-permissive\fR
Treat individual errors as non\-fatal
.TP
\fB\-m\fR, \fB\-\-mini\-mode\fR
Called from the rpmlint\-mini wrapper (SUSE\-only)
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fR \fI<format>\fR
Report output format: human\-readable text (default) or machine\-readable JSON (upstream rpmlint#1156). Overrides the `OutputFormat` config key
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
text
.IP \(bu 2
json
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
[\fIrpmfile\fR]
RPMs / specfiles / directories to check
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
\fB0\fR
Clean run, or warnings and infos only. In the default permissive mode errors
scored at or under the threshold also exit 0, as do bare invocation,
\fB\-\-help\fR, \fB\-p\fR and \fB\-e\fR.
.TP
\fB2\fR
Nonexistent positional path or \fB\-c\fR path.
.TP
\fB3\fR
A package could not be read (reported; the run continues with the rest).
.TP
\fB4\fR
Unparsable TOML configuration.
.TP
\fB64\fR
\fB\-s\fR/\fB\-\-strict\fR was passed and an error was found.
.TP
\fB65\fR
\fB\-s\fR/\fB\-\-strict\fR was passed and every error was a strict promotion.
.TP
\fB66\fR
Badness score exceeded the threshold.
.TP
\fB130\fR
Interrupted (SIGINT).
.SH VERSION
v0.1.0
